# Environment template for the nested Next app (next/). Copy to next/.env.local for
# local-only overrides — .env.local is gitignored; NEVER commit a real secret.
#
# All values are OPTIONAL for local dev: sensible defaults exist, so an empty/absent file
# is a valid setup. The dev-time CMS content requires the sibling CMS running locally:
#
#   cd ../CMS_management-
#   bun run db:migrate:local   # once — creates/updates the local D1 tables
#   bun run dev                # serves the API at http://localhost:8080 (vite.config.ts)
#
# Without it, every CMS-backed section renders its approved static/model fallback and the
# server logs one redaction-safe [CMS] warning per endpoint.

# Server-only CMS base (FND-004). Default: http://localhost:8080/api/v1
# Production value is deployment-owned (MIG-010) — e.g. https://cms.thgfulfill.com/api/v1
#CMS_API_URL=

# Public site origin for canonical/hreflang/sitemap URLs (FND-003).
# Default: https://thgfulfill.com
#NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# Public CMS base for the lead-form island's client-side POST (WEB-001; public by design,
# parity with Vite's VITE_CMS_API_URL). Default: http://localhost:8080/api/v1
#NEXT_PUBLIC_CMS_API_URL=

# Cloudflare Turnstile site key (public). Empty → forms use the DEV_BYPASS token, which the
# CMS accepts only when its own TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY is also empty (local dev only).
#NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
